     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Sun, Nov 23, 2014 at 12:02 PM, somayeh shahba <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">so.s...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><div>Dear Philip, <br><br></div>I really tankful that you gave\r\n me reply. i used seven Likert scale in my questionnaire. and i don&#39;t \r\nknow how can i judge between difficulty for example table below is one \r\nof my items difficulty .would you please answer me which one is more \r\ndifficult intercept?<br></div></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div>I&#39;m not sure what you mean. The last category in a Likert is most difficult by definition since all categories are ordered. </div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><br>\r\n\r\n<div align=\"right\">\r\n\r\n<table dir=\"rtl\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;border:medium none\" height=\"61\" width=\"392\" border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\r\n <tbody><tr style=\"height:44.25pt\">\r\n  <td style=\"width:31.85pt;border:1pt solid windowtext;padding:0cm 5.4pt;height:44.25pt\" nowrap valign=\"top\" width=\"42\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"RTL\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:normal;direction:rtl\"><span dir=\"LTR\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;color:black\">2.035</span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td style=\"width:35.45pt;border-width:1pt medium 1pt 1pt;border-style:solid none solid solid;border-color:windowtext -moz-use-text-color windowtext windowtext;padding:0cm 5.4pt;height:44.25pt\" nowrap valign=\"top\" width=\"47\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"RTL\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:normal;direction:rtl\"><span dir=\"LTR\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;color:black\">0.272</span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td style=\"width:35.45pt;border-width:1pt medium 1pt 1pt;border-style:solid none solid solid;border-color:windowtext -moz-use-text-color windowtext windowtext;padding:0cm 5.4pt;height:44.25pt\" nowrap valign=\"top\" width=\"47\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"RTL\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:normal;direction:rtl\"><span dir=\"LTR\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;color:black\">-0.78</span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td style=\"width:35.4pt;border-width:1pt medium 1pt 1pt;border-style:solid none solid solid;border-color:windowtext -moz-use-text-color windowtext windowtext;padding:0cm 5.4pt;height:44.25pt\" nowrap valign=\"top\" width=\"47\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"RTL\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:normal;direction:rtl\"><span dir=\"LTR\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;color:black\">-1.81</span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td style=\"width:35.45pt;border-width:1pt medium 1pt 1pt;border-style:solid none solid solid;border-color:windowtext -moz-use-text-color windowtext windowtext;padding:0cm 5.4pt;height:44.25pt\" nowrap valign=\"top\" width=\"47\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"RTL\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:normal;direction:rtl\"><span dir=\"LTR\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;color:black\">-2.93</span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td style=\"width:35.45pt;border-width:1pt medium 1pt 1pt;border-style:solid none solid solid;border-color:windowtext -moz-use-text-color windowtext windowtext;padding:0cm 5.4pt;height:44.25pt\" nowrap valign=\"top\" width=\"47\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"RTL\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:normal;direction:rtl\"><span dir=\"LTR\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;color:black\">-4.6</span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n</tbody></table>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n\r\nAnd i Mean by question &quot;can we use regression or correlation between \r\nscores in order to test our Hypothesis?&quot; that when we use &quot;coef(mod1)&quot;  \r\nin MIRT package it gives us ability or trait ( <img alt=\"{\\theta}\" src=\"https://ci3.googleusercontent.com/proxy/9DoWfaVFnUYqYY1Oyr00Qc1CE32dxskah3_6fLPntaaLUuUT4B8dpsCov01K5FI_gVZq38yKqu8Kkv1u3iTuZBs7TJQjU5XHXoQlRNQ7pzKE5F-bUyX8OeqnSxhM4A=s0-d-e1-ft#http://upload.wikimedia.org/math/6/0/8/6083a03bd0bb5a107b32a5faec942099.png\">). </div></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div></div></div>"
